{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773771727,"nonce":"S7lihGM+fq8jPYTq0JJLpvzieII=","title":"Add -f (follow) flag to nightshift history command","message":"Add a `-f`/`--follow` flag to `nightshift history` that continuously watches the `conversation.jsonl` file and prints new entries as they appear, similar to `tail -f`.\n\nCurrent behavior: `nightshift history \u003cissue-id\u003e` prints all existing entries and exits.\n\nDesired behavior: `nightshift history -f \u003cissue-id\u003e` prints existing entries, then keeps watching for new lines and printing them in real-time until interrupted with Ctrl+C.\n\nImplementation notes:\n- Add `--follow`/`-f` argument to the history subparser in `_register_session_commands()`\n- In `cmd_history()`, after printing existing entries, if `a.follow` is True, enter a loop that watches for new lines (poll-based or inotify)\n- Simple approach: track file position, sleep briefly, read new lines, repeat\n- Format new entries the same way as existing ones (timestamp + icon + role + content)","files":null}]}